From cf51795bae01dc63675689f638d046b157940770 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Pfister <119864532+JJRPF@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:01:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t6020-j414s: enable PMP

Let m1n1 boot the Power Management Processor on the 14-inch MacBook Pro
(M2 Pro), as t6000-j314s does. With the PMP up, the fabric and DCS p-states
are the PMP's (pmgr-misc reports "PMP manages fabric and DCS p-states") and
the DCP, AVD and ISP power domains follow the PMP's report entries (pmp-disp0,
pmp-dispext0/1, pmp-isp-sys).

Measured on a J414s, headless, nothing attached, the same kernel with and
without the PMP, one boot each, 16 windows of 30 s: system power 3.485 W ->
2.566 W (-0.919 W), SoC (heatpipe) 1.990 W -> 1.341 W (-0.649 W). Held for a
1 h soak with the energy model on top: 2.36 W, 0 of 3695 pings lost, no new
kernel messages.

This needs an m1n1 that makes room for the PMP's tunables (81 properties,
about 16K, which the 96K device tree headroom does not hold on a T6020);
with an older m1n1 the boot stops in m1n1 proxy mode ("failed to transfer pmp tunable", no payload). Merge the
m1n1 change first. Suspend with the PMP on the J414s is not qualified here
(it is the S2R work in progress), so only enable this once that is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RuRMQncGu3ukpyW44vHHjQ
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6020-j414s.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6020-j414s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6020-j414s.dts
index a227069727dd..7a813db58d80 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6020-j414s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6020-j414s.dts
@@ -9,6 +9,12 @@
 
 /dts-v1/;
 
+/*
+ * Let m1n1 boot the PMP, which takes over the fabric and DCS p-states
+ * (needs an m1n1 that makes room for the PMP's tunables).
+ */
+#define APPLE_USE_PMP
+
 #include "t6020.dtsi"
 #include "t602x-j414-j416.dtsi"
 
